    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `format_for_display` in `app/report.py`, and all 5 tests pass with `pytest -q` (the 2 that were already there plus 3 new ones).\n\nIt formats each cell and returns a new table with the same index and columns, so the input is left unchanged. It uses only pandas, which was already a dependency.\n\n- `12500` \u2192 `\"12,500.00\"`\n- `-634.2` \u2192 `\"(634.20)\"`\n- zero \u2192 `\"-\"`\n- missing \u2192 `\"\"`\n\n**One choice you should know about:** values are rounded to two decimals before checking for zero. Anything that would print as `0.00` shows as `\"-\"`, including `-0.0`, tiny leftovers from adding up floats (like `1e-9`), and small negatives like `-0.004`. Without this, those values would show as `\"0.00\"` or `\"(0.00)\"`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_report.py`. It checks each rule against the sample ledger, the zero-after-rounding cases, and that the input table isn't changed."
